031e","position":{"commit_sha":"d9a10261a8f5543db198bdceed27fdd43f516d44","position":"1787644155574534001-c988b02b-220c-4273-a252-7ea3b58d031e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787028210057535001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b4ecb834-9a64-4e3a-85c1-c58a67cbdb58","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"d0ec-da23-32ba-47c6"},{"link_uuid":"d76e0355-1ee6-492e-8d60-6feb745368cd","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c83e-2c82-8dce-4c06"},{"link_uuid":"a754346a-b498-45f5-8ab0-c64464fa5b62","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7414-17fe-e27f-4136"},{"link_uuid":"f32ff35a-5ee0-4e6c-bfba-0b98bd4487e7","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"67d0-3330-a4ef-4382"}],"description":"## Context\nLegacy failure handling counts low-level physical noise (nested per-call retries) and has no endpoint-failure fuse that distinguishes an exhausted logical operation from its physical attempts; the only breaker today is the blast-radius mass-mutation guard `classify.check_blast_radius`, a different concern that is retained. The approved new scoped fuse must stop only demonstrably unhealthy scopes without terminating work that historical jobs completed.\n\n## Outcome\nImplement an endpoint/provider finite-pass fuse over normalized coordinator outcomes. Endpoint opens after three consecutive eligible exhausted logical outcomes across at least two tickets; provider additionally requires the failing outcomes to span >=2 distinct endpoints of the same provider. Matching success resets consecutive state.\n\n## Plan\n1. Count only exhausted logical outcomes eligible under the failure policy. Never count physical attempts, recovered warnings, permanent failures, ticket-local 404s, or opaque diagnostic text.\n2. Track endpoint consecutive outcomes and distinct tickets. Track provider scope only when failures span >=2 distinct endpoints of the same provider.\n3. Reset matching consecutive state on success; independent scopes retain their own state and continue.\n4. Preserve direct authoritative credential, configuration, quota, rate, issue, endpoint, tenant, provider, and global stop/defer behavior without inferring scope from text.\n5. When open, return explicit scope/reason/`retry_not_before` metadata; do not execute matching remaining plans.\n\n## Testing\nSequence tables pin threshold boundaries, exclusions, reset, two-ticket / two-distinct-endpoint requirements, and independent scopes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Endpoint fuse opens only after three consecutive eligible exhausted outcomes across at least two tickets.\n- [x] Provider fuse additionally requires the failing outcomes to span >=2 distinct endpoints of the same provider.\n- [x] A matching success resets the consecutive state.\n- [x] Physical attempts, recovered warnings, permanent failures, ticket-local 404s, and opaque diagnostics never increment inferred counters.\n- [x] Independent scopes continue when another scope opens.\n- [x] Open-fuse outcomes include exact scope, reason, and `retry_not_before`.\n\n## Out of scope\nProduction routing, batch tallies, and historical replay integration.\n## Fuse scope, eligibility & counter semantics (grounds E2/G6)\nNo new \"family\" concept — grounded entirely in existing types and the S3 T1 coordinator (now landed).\n- **Endpoint / provider.** *Endpoint* = one concrete provider instance an op is dispatched to (a single Jira base URL/site), the unit `operation_outcome.FailureScope.endpoint` already denotes; *provider* = the vendor behind >=1 endpoints (`FailureScope.provider`).\n- **Attribution.** `coordinator.TicketOutcome` carries `identity`, `disposition`, `failure_scope` but no endpoint id; the `(provider, endpoint)` identity for an outcome is resolved from the coordinator's `locate(identity)` binding mapping (the per-ticket binding it dispatched against). The fuse keys inferred counters off that resolved identity, NEVER off diagnostic text. A direct authoritative `failure_scope` of endpoint/tenant/provider/global still stops that scope immediately (step 4), independent of the inferred counter.\n- **Eligible exhausted outcome** — keyed off **budget-exhaustion provenance, not the disposition value**. The coordinator drives every transient retry through the shared per-op `retry_budget.RetryBudget`; an adapter first-attempt transient (`request_count=1`, `invocation_count=1`, `cumulative_sleep_ms=0`) is absorbed inside that retry loop and is never a pass outcome. An op is eligible only when the shared budget itself caps it: `plan_next_retry` returns `action=\"exhausted\"` (MAX_INVOCATIONS) -> `exhausted_transient`, or `action=\"defer\"` (would exceed `MAX_CUMULATIVE_SLEEP_MS` before MAX_INVOCATIONS) -> terminal `retryable_deferred` with `retry_not_before` and a consumed allowance (`invocation_count>1` or `cumulative_sleep_ms` at cap) — the slow/rate-limited mode that never surfaces `exhausted_transient`. The mid-loop `decide_replay(old_conclusive, budget_remaining=True)` (`replay=True`) is not a pass outcome. **Excluded**: `commit_unknown` (opaque/replay-forbidden), `recovered`, `already_satisfied`, `permanent_failure`, ticket-local 404, raw physical attempts, and any `retryable_deferred` the shared budget did not itself produce at its cap.\n- **Counter durability/order.** Per-pass, in-memory, per-scope; zeroed each `reconcile.py::reconcile_once(pass_id)` pass (no durable cross-pass state, consistent with S2's fresh Observation/version). \"Consecutive\" is per-scope over the coordinator's deterministic dependency-ordered execution; other scopes' interleaved outcomes neither increment nor reset a scope's counter (independent scopes continue). A same-scope success (`applied`/`recovered`/`already_satisfied`) resets that scope to zero.\n\n## Impacted sites (existing seams this change touches)\n- `coordinator.py` (landed S3 T1) — `TicketOutcome`/`CoordinationReport.outcome_for`/`coordinate(...)` supply per-outcome `(identity, disposition, failure_scope)`; `locate(identity)` binding resolves the `(provider, endpoint)` identity. The fuse consumes these; `coordinate` gains fuse-defer wiring additively.\n- `failure_policy.py` (landed S3 T1, 162 LOC) — `bucket_for` / `is_success` / `is_broad_scope` / `BROAD_SCOPES`; extended with the fuse-eligible-outcome predicate (budget-exhaustion provenance above). Watch 800-LOC cap.\n- `retry_budget.py` — `plan_next_retry` `action in {exhausted, defer}` is the eligibility provenance; consumed read-only.\n- `operation_outcome.py` — `Disposition` / `FailureScope` vocab, consumed unchanged.\n- `pass_fuse.py` (new) — the per-pass scoped fuse state machine and open/defer decision.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/pass_fuse.py","reason":"Endpoint/provider finite-pass fuse state and decisions."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/failure_policy.py","reason":"Declare fuse-eligible normalized outcomes and authoritative scopes."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_scoped_pass_fuse.py","reason":"Threshold, diversity, reset, exclusion, and isolation sequences."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","d0ec-da23-32ba-47c6"],["parent","28a3-a62d-6345-44a0"],["relates_to","67d0-3330-a4ef-4382"],["relates_to","7414-17fe-e27f-4136"],["relates_to","c83e-2c82-8dce-4c06"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"28a3-a62d-6345-44a0","parent_status_uuid":"5077ad22-c486-4753-9c50-b0b4eaded40a","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["rp03","fuse","retry","tdd"],"ticket_id":"dd65-54fa-f4c3-4bc9","ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-03 S3 T2 — Implement the scoped finite-pass fuse","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_scoped_pass_fuse.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC6","dd_text":"Endpoint/provider thresholds, reset, exclusions, independent scope, and deferral metadata"}]},"source_event_uuids":["398863db-a3b1-42ec-bdc1-9414b346f86d","2e2a8bf4-7b1f-41f9-956b-3398e8150530","91442be6-80fe-4714-a60c-0b139dcdecdd","ce93837c-5915-4eb4-a81e-daf435b5e044","307e6549-9d3e-42e3-a38a-ab3d31a1fa86","36d81c8a-1d14-4011-aa9c-dcdc811d9218","d76e0355-1ee6-492e-8d60-6feb745368cd","a754346a-b498-45f5-8ab0-c64464fa5b62","f32ff35a-5ee0-4e6c-bfba-0b98bd4487e7","d79c28c5-8a7f-45de-ba65-014d5d778b80","5077ad22-c486-4753-9c50-b0b4eaded40a","c988b02b-220c-4273-a252-7ea3b58d031e"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787649979522285001,"uuid":"163d0f5c-44fe-4fce-bf8a-56b5c838b2a5"}